  "Question": "If \\(\\log x-5\\log3=-2,\\) then \\(x\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1.25\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.81\\)",
    "C": "\\(2.43\\)",
    "D": "\\(0.8\\)",
    "E": "either \\(0.8\\) or \\(1.25\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Use the common-logarithm convention: \\(\\log\\) has base \\(10\\), and its argument requires \\(x>0\\). The power and quotient rules let us combine the left side into one logarithm:\n\\[\n\\log x-5\\log3\n=\\log x-\\log(3^5)\n=\\log\\left(\\frac{x}{243}\\right).\n\\]\nThus \\(\\log(x/243)=-2\\). By the definition of a base-10 logarithm,\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{243}=10^{-2}=\\frac1{100},\n\\qquad\nx=\\frac{243}{100}=2.43.\n\\]\nThese transformations are reversible for \\(x>0\\), and the resulting value is positive. Therefore \\(x=2.43\\), choice C.",
